@vindex vm-forwarding-subject-format
String which specifies the format of the contents of the Subject
header that is generated for a forwarded message.  See the documentation
for the variable @code{vm-summary-format} for information on what this string
may contain.  The format should *not* end with nor contain a newline.
Nil means leave the Subject header empty when forwarding.

Default value: @code{"forwarded message from %F"}
@end defopt

@end macro

@macro vmdocvmresendbounceddiscardheaderregexp
@defopt vm-resend-bounced-discard-header-regexp
@vindex vm-resend-bounced-discard-header-regexp
Non-nil value should be a regular expression that tells
what headers should not appear in a resent bounced message.  This
variable along with @code{vm-resend-bounced-headers} determines which headers
are kept and which headers are discarded.

If the value of @code{vm-resend-bounced-discard-header-regexp} is nil,
the headers matched by @code{vm-resend-bounced-headers} are the only
headers that will be kept.

If @code{vm-resend-bounced-discard-header-regexp} is non-nil, then only
headers matched by this variable will be discarded; all others
will be kept.  @code{vm-resend-bounced-headers} determines the order of
appearance in that case, with headers not matching any in the
@code{vm-resend-bounced-headers} list appearing last in the headers of
the message.
@end defopt

@end macro

@macro vmdocvmresendbouncedheaders
@defopt vm-resend-bounced-headers
@vindex vm-resend-bounced-headers
List of headers that should be appear in messages resent with
@code{vm-resend-bounced-message}.  These should be listed in the order you wish them
to appear in the message.  Regular expressions are allowed.
There is no need to anchor patterns with "^", as searches always
start at the beginning of a line.  Put a colon at the end of
patterns to get exact matches.  (E.g. "Date" matches "Date"
and "Date-Sent".)  Header names are always matched case
insensitively.

If the value of @code{vm-resend-bounced-discard-header-regexp} is nil, the headers
matched by @code{vm-resend-bounced-headers} are the only headers that will be
kept.

If @code{vm-resend-bounced-discard-header-regexp} is non-nil, then only
headers matched by that variable will be discarded; all others
will be kept.  @code{vm-resend-bounced-headers} determines the order of
appearance in that case, with headers not matching any in the
@code{vm-resend-bounced-headers} list appearing last in the headers of
the message.

Default value:
@example
("MIME-Version:" "Content-" "From:" "Sender:" "Reply-To:" "To:"
 "Newsgroups:" "Cc:" "Subject:" "Newsgroups:" "In-Reply-To:"
 "References:" "Keywords:" "X-")
@end example
@end defopt

@end macro

@macro vmdocvmresenddiscardheaderregexp
@defopt vm-resend-discard-header-regexp
