@macro vmdocvmattachfilesindirectorydefaultcharset
@defopt vm-attach-files-in-directory-default-charset
@vindex vm-attach-files-in-directory-default-charset
The default charset used for attached files of type @code{text}.
If set to nil you will be asked for the charset.
If set to @code{guess} it will be determined by @code{vm-determine-proper-charset}, but
this may take some time, since the file needs to be visited.

Default value: @code{guess}
@end defopt

@end macro

@macro vmdocvmattachfilesindirectorydefaulttype
@defopt vm-attach-files-in-directory-default-type
@vindex vm-attach-files-in-directory-default-type
The default MIME-type for attached files.
If set to nil you will be asked for the type if it cannot be guessed.
For guessing mime-types we use @code{vm-mime-attachment-auto-type-alist}.
@end defopt

@end macro

@macro vmdocvmautodecodemimemessages
@defopt vm-auto-decode-mime-messages
@vindex vm-auto-decode-mime-messages
Non-nil value causes MIME decoding to occur automatically
when a message containing MIME objects is exposed.  A nil value
means that you will have to run the @code{vm-decode-mime-message}
command (normally bound to @code{D}) manually to decode and display
MIME objects.

Default value: @code{t}
@end defopt

@end macro

@macro vmdocvmautosaveallattachments
@defopt vm-auto-save-all-attachments
@vindex vm-auto-save-all-attachments
Non-nil means save the attachments of a message as it arrives.
@code{vm-mime-auto-save-all-attachments} does the saving, under
@code{vm-mime-attachment-save-directory} in a subdirectory named by
@code{vm-mime-auto-save-all-attachments-subdir}.
@end defopt

@end macro

@macro vmdocvmdisplayusingmime
@defopt vm-display-using-mime
@vindex vm-display-using-mime
Non-nil value means VM should display messages using MIME.
MIME (Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions) is a set of
extensions to the standard Internet message format that allows
reliable transmission and reception of arbitrary data including
images, audio and video as well as ordinary text.

A non-nil value for this variable means that VM will recognize
MIME encoded messages and display them as specified by the
various MIME standards specifications.

A nil value means VM will not display MIME messages any
differently than any other message.

Default value: @code{t}
@end defopt

@end macro

@macro vmdocvmemitmessagesformimedecoding
@defopt vm-emit-messages-for-mime-decoding
@vindex vm-emit-messages-for-mime-decoding
Flag to allow minibuffer messages about the progress of MIME
decoding of messages.  Only nontrivial decodings are normally
reported.  So there is normally no need to change this from the default.

Default value: @code{t}
@end defopt

@end macro

@macro vmdocvmicalendardescriptionlines
@defopt vm-icalendar-description-lines
@vindex vm-icalendar-description-lines
