@code{vm-postpone-message-hook} is the one that runs before, where a change still
reaches the folder.
@end defopt

@end macro

@macro vmdocvmsavekilledmessage
@defopt vm-save-killed-message
@vindex vm-save-killed-message
What killing a composition with writing in it does with the writing.

@code{always}, the default, files it in @code{vm-save-killed-messages-folder} and says
so.  Nothing is lost by killing a composition, which is what a reader who has
lost drafts to a keystroke needs (emacs-vm/vm#824).

@code{ask} asks whether to keep it.  Nil neither keeps it nor asks, and then
@code{vm-confirm-killing-a-composition} is what stands between a keystroke and the
writing.

A composition nothing has been written in is not kept and is not asked about,
whichever this is.

Default value: @code{always}
@end defopt

@end macro

