@macro vmdocvmtoolbarprintcommand
@deffn Command vm-toolbar-print-command &optional count
@findex vm-toolbar-print-command
Print the current message
Prefix arg N means print the current message and the next N - 1 messages.
Prefix arg -N means print the current message and the previous N - 1 messages.

The variable @code{vm-print-command} controls what command is run to
print the message, and @code{vm-print-command-switches} is a list of switches
to pass to the command.

When invoked on marked messages (via @code{vm-next-command-uses-marks}),
each marked message is printed, one message per vm-print-command
invocation.  If applied to collapsed threads in summary and thread
operations are enabled via @code{vm-enable-thread-operations} then all messages
in the thread are printed.

Output, if any, is displayed.  The message is not altered.

@emph{Not autoloaded}: VM has to be loaded before @kbd{M-x} offers this one.
@end deffn

@end macro

@macro vmdocvmtoolbarquitcommand
@deffn Command vm-toolbar-quit-command &optional no-expunge no-change
@findex vm-toolbar-quit-command
Quit visiting the current folder, saving changes.  If the folder is
being visited read-only then changes are not saved.  This behavior
can be customized using @code{vm-preserve-read-only-folders-on-disk}.

If the customization variable @code{vm-expunge-before-quit} is set to
  non-nil value then deleted messages are expunged.

Giving a prefix argument overrides the variable and no expunge is
done.

When called internally, the optional argument NO-EXPUNGE says
that the deleted messages should not be expunged (irrespective of
the value of @code{vm-expunge-before-quit}.  NO-CHANGE says that
changes should be discarded.

@emph{Not autoloaded}: VM has to be loaded before @kbd{M-x} offers this one.
@end deffn

